  "novel_mechanics_found": "The unexplained 8x8 color-1 glyph is a collision-based deformation fixture, not decoration or a paint swatch. When a composite piece is pushed into it, individual strokes are pinned while the rest moves, reshaping a plus asymmetrically or trading rectangle width for height. On level 6 this converted the 19x19 color-11 outline first to 4x34, then\u2014after routing below the fixture\u2014to the required 10x28 outline. Level 7 adds five top-edge paint swatches (9, 11, 8, 14, 6) and three overlapping selectable pieces; touching the 9 swatch repainted the selected color-10 plus to 9.",
  "narrative": "Resolved and replayed the exact 276-action banked prefix from results/outer_loop_fable5_re86_probe.json; the fresh live environment reached frame.levels_completed=5 as required. Frame-only analysis of level 6 identified four color-9 targets for an asymmetric plus and four color-11 targets for a 10x28 rectangle. I used the central color-1 fixture to deform and place both pieces, observing the live win at action 341 (5 -> 6), then ran reproduce() from a fresh reset on the full 341-action sequence; it reached level 6 and returned reproduced=true. The final 18 calls mapped level 7 selection order and confirmed repainting at the 9 swatch. I stopped because the strict session total was exactly 700 calls (341 live plus 341 gate plus 18 level-7 exploration).",
  "gotchas": [
    "The central 8x8 color-1 object is load-bearing: collision can pin one stroke of a composite piece while other strokes keep moving, thereby changing geometry.",
    "For the level-6 color-9 targets at (12,6), (9,9), (30,9), and (12,27), the plus must be made asymmetric; a symmetric placement cannot cover all four.",
    "For the level-6 color-11 targets at (45,30), (54,30), (45,57), and (54,57), reshape the 19x19 outline to 10x28. A useful route squeezes it to 4x34 against the fixture, moves below the fixture, then squeezes vertically to 10x28 before translating to the targets.",
    "The black pixel is the selection marker. On level 7 ACTION5 cycles color-10 plus -> color-12 outline -> color-7 plus -> color-10 plus.",
    "Level 7 has five framed paint swatches along the top edge with fill colors 9, 11, 8, 14, and 6. Fifteen ACTION1 presses from the initial color-10-plus position touch the 9 swatch and repaint that piece.",
    "Row 63 is the per-level move bar and may visually occlude off-board or bottom-edge piece pixels; account for it when inferring a deformed outline.",
    "Rendered frame buffers mutate in place, so copy grids before computing action diffs."
  ],
  "solve_provenance": "live_agent_self_discovery"
